\subsection{Measurement Update and MEKF Reset}
\label{sec:meas-update-structure}

Each IMU step propagates the nominal quaternion and covariance, applies a
due integral pseudo-update, then corrects with the accelerometer. Magnetic
updates are asynchronous. Each accepted correction includes injection/reset.
All three channels have three-component innovations; the magnetic Jacobian
has rank two, while the accelerometer and integral selectors have rank three.  For
\[
\vct{z}=h(\vct{x})+\vct{\nu},
\qquad
\vct{\nu}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mat{R}),
\qquad
\mat{C}=\left.\frac{\partial h}{\partial\delta\vct{x}}\right|_{\hat{\vct{x}}^-},
\]
define
\begin{align}
\vct{r}&=\vct{z}-h(\hat{\vct{x}}^-),\\
\matg{\Lambda}&=\mat{C}\mat{P}^-\mat{C}^{\top}+\mat{R},\\
\mat{K}&=\mat{P}^-\mat{C}^{\top}\matg{\Lambda}^{-1}.
\label{eq:kalman-gain}
\end{align}
The error-state and Joseph covariance updates are
\begin{equation}
\delta\hat{\vct{x}}^+=\delta\hat{\vct{x}}^-+\mat{K}\vct{r},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\mat{P}^+=(\Id-\mat{K}\mat{C})\mat{P}^-(\Id-\mat{K}\mat{C})^{\top}
+\mat{K}\mat{R}\mat{K}^{\top}.
\label{eq:joseph-update}
\end{equation}

\subsubsection{Three-component correction structure}
Partition
\[
\delta\vct{x}=[\vct{A}^{\top},\vct{L}^{\top},\vct{B}^{\top}]^{\top},
\]
where $\vct{A}\in\mathbb{R}^6$,
$\vct{L}=[\delta\vct{v},\delta\vct{p},\delta\vct{S},
\delta\vct{a}_w]\in\mathbb{R}^{12}$, and
$\vct{B}=\delta\vct{b}_a\in\mathbb{R}^3$.  Each correction therefore requires
the $3\times3$ innovation solve of Eq.~\eqref{eq:kalman-gain}, while
cross-covariances can update state groups not directly selected by $\mat C$.
The accelerometer, magnetometer, and integral-channel Jacobians are given by
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:acc-meas-jacobians}, \eqref{eq:mag-meas-jacobian}, and
\eqref{eq:HS-selector}, respectively, with columns ordered as in
\eqref{eq:state-vector}.

\subsubsection{Nominal-state injection and quaternion reset}
After an accepted correction, additive states are injected as
\begin{align}
\hat{\vct{b}}_g &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{b}}_g+\delta\hat{\vct{b}}_g,&
\hat{\vct{v}} &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{v}}+\delta\hat{\vct{v}},\\
\hat{\vct{p}} &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{p}}+\delta\hat{\vct{p}},&
\hat{\vct{S}} &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{S}}+\delta\hat{\vct{S}},\\
\hat{\vct{a}}_w &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{a}}_w+\delta\hat{\vct{a}}_w,&
\hat{\vct{b}}_a &\leftarrow \hat{\vct{b}}_a+\delta\hat{\vct{b}}_a.
\label{eq:additive-state-injection}
\end{align}
The left-multiplicative quaternion injection
then uses
\begin{equation}
q\leftarrow\exp_q\!\left(\tfrac12\delta\hat{\vct{\theta}}\right)\otimes q.
\label{eq:quat-error-injection}
\end{equation}
Because this changes local attitude coordinates, simply setting
$\delta\hat{\vct\theta}=0$ is not covariance consistent.  To first order,
\begin{equation}
\mat{G}_{\theta}
=\Id+\tfrac12\Skew{\delta\hat{\vct{\theta}}},
\qquad
\mat{G}_{\mathrm{reset}}
=\blkdiag(\mat{G}_{\theta},\Id_{N_X-3}),
\label{eq:left-reset-jacobian}
\end{equation}
followed by
\begin{equation}
\mat{P}^+
\leftarrow
\mat{G}_{\mathrm{reset}}\mat{P}^+
\mat{G}_{\mathrm{reset}}^{\top},
\qquad
\delta\hat{\vct{\theta}}\leftarrow0.
\label{eq:mekf-reset-covariance}
\end{equation}
This transformation applies to the attitude marginal and all attitude
cross-covariances whenever a correction induces nonzero attitude error.

\subsubsection{Horizontal wave displacement and velocity at the output}
The OU--III sketch reports horizontal wave motion about the vessel's cruise
track. For a harmonic displacement with angular frequency $\omega$, its
zero-mean primitive $S$ and its velocity $v$ satisfy $S+v/\omega^2=0$.
In an irregular sea the filter estimates a coefficient $\beta$ from the ratio
of horizontal displacement variance to horizontal velocity variance. Each
variance is half the trace of the centered north/east covariance accumulated
with an exponential time constant of eight encounter periods. The ratio is
bounded to $[0.25,4](T/2\pi)^2$ using the applied encounter period $T$.
The centered variance of $S+\beta v$ supplies a scalar noise variance $r$
that allows for the width of the encounter spectrum.

Let $C$ select $S_H+\beta v_H$ from the state, with subscript $H$ denoting
the two horizontal components. From the current posterior $(x,P)$
the reported horizontal displacement and velocity are
\begin{equation}
 \begin{bmatrix}p_H\\v_H\end{bmatrix}_{\!\rm wave}
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}p_H\\v_H\end{bmatrix}
 - w\,P_{(p_H,v_H),:}C^\top (CPC^\top+rI_2)^{-1}
      (S_H+\beta v_H).
 \label{eq:horizontal-wave-readout}
\end{equation}
Accumulation starts in Live with accelerometer-bias updates enabled and a
usable period. The blend $w$ rises linearly from zero to one between the
third and fourth accumulated cycles. The implementation solves the two by
two system at readout time, including magnetic corrections received since
the last IMU sample. The recursive state and covariance feed the next
prediction. Section~\ref{sec:wave-readout-replay} evaluates the reported
wave motion on held-out sensor draws.

\subsubsection{Numerical invariants}
The innovation matrix uses an LDL$^{\top}$ solve with a scale-dependent diagonal
safeguard only when needed.  The Joseph update, covariance symmetrization, and
MEKF reset preserve $\mat P=\mat P^\top$, $\mat P\succeq0$, unit quaternion
norm, and zero local attitude-error mean to numerical precision.
